{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Physical Database Structures"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words that you can use when describing components or database structures."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to query analysis, and data base engines.  Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level. \tRecognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "take a while "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short period of time that must pass before something is finished"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The datafile could take a while to be created."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "get around "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Control files contain the entries that help to get around the physical structure."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "as a matter of fact "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in fact"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As a matter of fact, I do."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "advisable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something good and people recommend it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's advisable to have archived copies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ease "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the simplicity of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can store and manage the data with ease."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "go hand in hand "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "two people or items that are and work well together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They usually go hand in hand with the alert and trace log files."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Negative Questions to Suggest and Idea"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to be polite or suggest and idea, you can use <span class=\"strong\">negative tag questions</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Negative questions</strong> are a way to suggest and idea or to confirm information. You usually make a statement followed then by the negative question. </br></br> Example</br><span class=\"italic\"> We need to buy more soda,<strong> don't we?</strong></span> </br></br>  These are the requirements for a negative tag question: </br> -\tThe statement has to be affirmative: </br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">Carlos <strong>runs</strong> every morning, <strong>doesn't</strong> he?</span> </br></br>  -\tIt has to keep the tense of the original statement. </br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">Vicky<strong> enjoys</strong> the snow, <strong>doesn't</strong> she?</span> </br></br>  -\tThe auxiliary verb will depend on the verb used in the statement:  </br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">They <strong>will</strong> buy the snacks, <strong>won't </strong>they?</span> </br>                  <span class=\"italic\">Miguel <strong>can</strong> speak English, <strong>can't</strong> he?</span> </br></br>  Finally, make sure you're using the correct subject pronoun for your tag question which has to be the subject of the statement. </br><span class=\"italic\"><strong>Vanessa</strong> </strong>did her homework, didn't <strong>she</strong>?</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's get through them one by one, so we can keep up with all this information, can't we?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you say other files, you are talking about the redo logs, aren't you?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Phrasal verbs</strong> are verbs composed of two words that have different meanings when they are separated. There are some phrasal verbs that are separable and there are some others which are inseparable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Phrasal verbs </strong>are verbs composed of two or more words. For example:</br></br>  Turn: rotate</br> Up: that points towards or higher</br> Turn up: increase the volume of a stereo</br></br>  This phrasal verb can be broken into two without affecting its meaning:</br> <span class=\"italic\">I'll <strong>turn up</strong> the volume.</span> </br> <span class=\"italic\">I'll <strong>turn</strong> the volume<strong> up</strong></span>.</br></br>  On the contrary, there are some <strong>phrasal verbs</strong> called \u201cinseparable\u201d because the words can never be set apart. </br></br>  Examples</br><strong> (correct) </strong> <span class=\"italic\">   I <strong>came across</strong> a coin when I went to the bank.</span> </br> <strong> (incorrect)</strong><span class=\"italic\"> I <strong>came</strong> a coin <strong>across </strong>I went to the bank.</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"back up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"support\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"count on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"depend\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get rid of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"eliminate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"keep up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"working to be at the same level than someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get around \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to move around\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get through\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to overcome a difficult situation\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's get through them one by one, so we can keep up with all this information "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Control files contain the entries that help to get around the physical structure"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Alert and Trace Log Files"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Every procedure in the server including a background process can be copied to an associated trace file. Whenever an error shows up during a process, information about that error is released to its trace file. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is necessary to know that part of that information is shared with the database administrator as well as the support service. Trace files produce alert logs or files inside databases in a chronological log of messages. The mechanisms that play an important role in the collection of the trace are the Automatic Diagnostic Repository (ADR) and the Incident Packaging Service (IPS). The first one controls and organizes trace files by providing a critical view of critical errors and producing a possible resolution. The second one takes data related to critical errors from ADR and sends them to the support services."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about physical database structures. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe each one and its usefulness.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a 200 word text explaining each one, using the grammar. studied. Don't forget to add examples to support your ideas. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your work with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for more information about physical database structures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a descriptive text. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss my work with my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mark</span>: Remembering all the components of physical structures is hard!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam</span>: Let's get through them one by one, so we can keep up with all this information, don't you think so?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mark</span>: Ok. I recall that datafiles contain all the data. One datafile can only be associated with a tablespace, which helps to organize all the files, and grants people to have easy access to them. When we modify or create new data, it remains in the memory before going to the definitive datafiles; these files are called temporary files or tempfiles.</br>"}, {"time": "35000", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sam</span>: In contrast, I know that control files contain the entries that help to get around the physical structure; they control the other type of files to proceed. They have the database name, locations, and timestamps of other files.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mark</span>: When you say other files, you are talking about the redo logs, right?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam</span>: Exactly! You wouldn't happen to know about the redo logs files, would you?"}, {"time": "60500", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mark</span>: As a matter of fact, I do. They record all the changes that we made in the data, so if there is a failure or we delete a file, we can back them up. The redo log files are always online, but it's advisable to have archived copies, also called offline copies. I understand all that, but I have trouble grasping the parameter files, don't you have them too?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam</span>: No, I don't. They may seem confusing, but they are not. Parameter files simply configure databases, so you can store and manage the data with ease. They usually go hand in hand with the alert and trace log files; when there is that much information, it is really common that errors occur. These files do not fix the errors, they only help you to locate and view them.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mark</span>: Well, the components aren't hard to recall, but the easiest ones to remember are the backup files."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le03ob02re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le03ob02re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 2, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list some components in physical database structures.  "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you organize huge amounts of data in databases when creating a project?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What can you do to organize the data with ease?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about characteristics of some components in physical database structures."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner."}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "The Physical Database Structures"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [2], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Mark can't remember the physical database structures' characteristics."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "conte